  <section class="hub-section hub-section-gray">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <h2>How our techs approach commercial holding cabinets</h2>
      <p>Hot-holding cabinets fail in predictable ways: thermostat drift (the cabinet runs 5-10°F off set-point), heating element burnout (one zone goes cold while others stay hot), humidity-control failure on the more sophisticated Alto-Shaam units, and door-seal degradation that lets heat leak and forces the unit to over-cycle. We diagnose the failure mode first, confirm with a temperature probe at multiple cabinet positions, and quote the repair. Most service items we carry on the truck. The Alto-Shaam cook-and-hold integration (their proofing-into-holding workflow) is unique in this category — we're factory-trained on that specific service tree and don't outsource it.</p>
    </div>
