          <summary>Is Alto-Shaam still the gold standard for holding cabinets?</summary>
          <p>Yes, in our experience. Their thermostat accuracy and humidity-control integration is meaningfully better than competitors at the institutional level. That said, Hatco countertop drawers and Cres Cor mobile cabinets are equally appropriate for their specific use cases (counter service prep, mobile catering). The choice is scope-driven.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>My holding cabinet runs cold on one shelf. What's wrong?</summary>
          <p>Almost always a heating element burnout on that shelf circuit. Less commonly: a thermostat sensor drifted in that zone. We test element resistance on each circuit, confirm sensor accuracy with a calibrated probe, and replace whichever has failed. About a $245-$385 repair on most cabinets.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item">
          <summary>Do holding cabinets need annual service?</summary>
          <p>Yes, especially for health-code compliance. We recommend an annual thermostat calibration check, door-seal inspection, and a humidity-control verification on units that have it. Documented annual service supports your food-safety records.</p>
        </details>
